  {
    "sha": "15816fe1cbbb7f84f6a53ae0617b3189b3be1fd0",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDE1ODE2ZmUxY2JiYjdmODRmNmE1M2FlMDYxN2IzMTg5YjNiZTFmZDA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T20:58:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T20:58:54Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui,app): an async file picker opens models and projects in the browser\n\nThe browser build (wasm32) had no way to open anything: every picker\nanswered \"cancelled\". File > Open model and Open project now ask a\nbrowser <input type=file> (ui::file_pick) and return at once; the file's\nname and bytes reach an inbox that State::drain_actions takes each frame\nas CommandKind::OpenPicked. A model lands through the new\nImportModel::from_bytes (the path import's laws - IGES/unknown extension,\nsize cap, STEP budget bounds, finite-mesh gate - shared through\nchecked_budget) and finish_import, so it is one undo step; a project\nthrough project::open_noted. A failed read, a file over the 256 MiB\nbrowser read limit, a refused import or a non-text project is said on the\nstatus line by name. Native builds keep rfd's synchronous dialogs; their\ninbox stays empty.\n\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
